From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] wifi: rtw88: sdio: power the MAC off at shutdown

A warm reboot leaves an SDIO chip powered, and on boards where WL_REG_ON is
not wired to the host nothing else takes power off it either: on the Denver
TAQ-102 the pwrseq reset line (gpio2 PB5), the BT enable line and every
switchable RK816 LDO were toggled by hand on a wedged RTL8723CS and the
chip still enumerated with its old firmware running. The next probe then
finds the MAC on, rtw_mac_power_on takes the -EALREADY path, and the
power-on sequence never sees power-ready: "failed to poll offset=0x6
mask=0x2 value=0x2", "mac power on failed", no wlan0 until a full
power-off.

rtw_sdio_shutdown only ran the chip's own shutdown op, which 8703b does not
have. Take the ifdown path instead when the interface is running: it ends in
rtw_power_off and leaves the chip in card-disable state, which the next
boot's power-on sequence handles. rtw_pci_shutdown does the equivalent with
PCI_D3hot.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Deluxe <info@busirocket.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
index 5b40d74b1..ce124e603 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/sdio.c
@@ -1434,6 +1434,18 @@ void rtw_sdio_shutdown(struct sdio_func *sdio_func)
 
 	if (chip->ops->shutdown)
 		chip->ops->shutdown(rtwdev);
+
+	/* Power the MAC off before the reboot. A warm reboot leaves the chip
+	 * powered on SDIO boards, and where WL_REG_ON is not wired to the host
+	 * the firmware keeps running through it; the next probe then finds the
+	 * MAC already on and its power-on sequence never sees power-ready
+	 * (offset 0x6 bit 1). Take the same path as bringing the interface
+	 * down, which leaves the chip in card-disable state.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&rtwdev->mutex);
+	if (test_bit(RTW_FLAG_RUNNING, rtwdev->flags))
+		rtw_core_stop(rtwdev);
+	mutex_unlock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(rtw_sdio_shutdown);
 
